[directions] d-06 [open] Build the final quantitative DW exclusion: f_s=1 line from s; d-07 [open] Cross-check thermal-relic to DW sterile mass mapping and qua; d-08 [open] Verify Lyman-alpha WDM systematics and Planck tension claims
[phase] critic-plan
[usage]
[critique] wave 0 plan: revise
[directions] d-06 [open] Build the final quantitative DW exclusion: f_s=1 line from s; d-07 [open] Cross-check thermal-relic to DW sterile mass mapping and qua; d-08 [open] Verify Lyman-alpha WDM systematics and Planck tension claims; d-09 [open] Quantify BBN/CMB Delta N_eff and Yp/D/H shifts for DW grid a
**Plan.** Four lines of investigation.

1. Build the final quantitative DW exclusion: f_s=1 line from sterile-nu tools vs Lyman-alpha mapped floors and digitized X-ray sin^2(2theta) limits, with binding constraint per mass. D-01 computed f_s=1 mixings (3.95e-11 at 20 keV to 9.17e-12 at 45 keV) and showed tool X-ray flag is sparse; d-04 showed literature X-ray limits exist only as figures and were not digitized; d-05 showed tool normalisation is 3-16x higher than Abazajian/ALS. The core deliverable - allowed DW fraction vs m_s with Lyman-alpha vs X-ray binding - is still missing (x-02, x-04, q-06).
2. Cross-check thermal-relic to DW sterile mass mapping and quantify floor spread from alternative prescriptions. D-03 verified Viel et al. 2005 Eq.5 (m_s=4.43 keV*(m_WDM/1keV)^4/3) and computed floors 20.2/21.9/29.3/45.4 keV for 3.1/3.3/4.1/5.7 keV, but second mapping, spread, and <p/T> check were blocked (x-03, q-08). Published limits quote different coefficients (4-5 keV) and half-mode vs free-streaming matching differ by ~10-20%.
3. Verify Lyman-alpha WDM systematics and Planck tension claims against full texts with citable quotes. D-02 verified 2309.04533 >5.7 keV (k_max=0.2 s/km) / 4.1 keV (k_max<0.1) and 1702.01764 combined 5.3 keV (3.5 keV with T jumps) but only from abstracts for 2209.14220,1306.2314,1702.01764; k_max, thermal-history priors, peculiar-velocity/inhomogeneous reionization systematics and SDSS DR14+Planck tension (1911.09073, Rogers & Poulin) remain unchecked.
4. Quantify BBN/CMB Delta N_eff and Yp/D/H shifts for DW grid and test eV-scale SBL anomaly thermalization control. Brief requires Delta N_eff at BBN/CMB, Yp and D/H vs Delta N_eff, and SBL anomaly check as reproducible analyses. Current d-06/d-07/d-08 do not call scan_sterile_nu_parameters, plot_sterile_nu_bbn_impact, check_sterile_nu_sbl_anomaly, or systematic predict_sterile_nu_xray_line, leaving core sterile-nu tool validation uncovered. Added by the critic.

The critic asked for changes:
- Budget overrun: 3x get_paper_figures (2207.04572, 1908.09037, 1609.00667) + predict_sterile_nu_grid + predict_sterile_nu + predict_sterile_nu_xray_line + describe_sterile_nu_tools + read_arxiv_chunk + cite + plot_sterile_nu_exclusion + list_agent_files = 11+ calls >10. Reduce to 2 X-ray sources (prioritize 2207.04572 NuSTAR 6-40 keV and 1908.09037 Fig.5) or split digitization to separate job.
- Unverifiable f_s,max_Xray if single normalisation used: tool f_s=1 mixings 3.95e-11 at 20 keV to 9.17e-12 at 45 keV are 3-16x higher than Abazajian/ALS per d-05. Must compute f_s,max_Xray = sin^2_Xray / sin^2(f_s=1) for both normalisations and verify linear Omega_s h^2 scaling at low mixing with predict_sterile_nu_grid at 1e-12, otherwise binding-constraint claim is not reproducible.
- Feasibility: read_text_file for astro-ph/0501562 will fail - list_input_files and list_agent_files are empty, no local papers. Must use web_search + read_arxiv_chunk for Viel 2005 Eq.5 and Abazajian astro-ph/0512631. Also describe_sterile_nu_tools does not output transfer function k_1/2/k_hm; tool free-streaming length comparison is analytic-only and must be flagged as such.
