**Blocked — Cross-check thermal-relic to DW sterile mass mapping and quantify floor spread from alternative prescriptions.** Tool budget exhausted after 4 calls (3x predict_sterile_nu + 1x get_paper_figures); no read_text_file/read_arxiv_chunk executed to quote-verify Viel Eq.5 or extract Abazajian alternative coefficients, and web_search DNS failed. Direction d-07 asked to cross-check the thermal-relic warm dark matter (WDM, a light thermal particle that erases small-scale structure) to Dodelson-Widrow sterile neutrino (DW, non-resonant oscillation production) mass mapping and quantify spread. Tool budget (4 calls) was reached before full text could be read, so success criteria were not met. What was established: sterile-neutrino tool free-streaming lengths (the distance particles stream and erase structure) are 53.2 kpc at 20.2 keV, 36.7 kpc at 29.3 keV, and 23.7 kpc at 45.4 keV, scaling inversely with mass as expected, all in warm dark matter regime with valid Big Bang Nucleosynthesis (BBN, light-element formation) treatment. For these DW masses at mixing sin^2 2theta =1e-10, BBN impact is negligible: extra radiation Delta N_eff =0.0014 to 0.0027 (total N_eff 3.045 to 3.047, where 3.044 is standard), helium mass fraction Yp =0.2468 to 0.2469 (observed 0.2449 +-0.004) and deuterium D/H x1e5 =2.44 (observed 2.547 +-0.025), Delta chi^2 vs standard model -0.02 to -0.04, allowed at 95% confidence, so BBN does not constrain these masses. Viel et al. 2005 (astro-ph/0501562) transfer function T(k) (how power is suppressed vs wavenumber k) calibration was partially extracted: Figure 28-29 (Fig 1) shows T(k) from Eq.4 for 92-1441 eV thermal masses with Eq.7 analytic fits, Figure 30 (Fig 2) shows flux power suppression for 0.5-8 keV at z=2.5-4, Figure 31 (Fig 3) shows bias function, files at /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-lyman-wdm/runs/261107_183057/figures_astro-ph_0501562/fig01_1.png etc. What remains open: quote-verified Viel Eq.5 coefficient 4.43 keV and exponents 4/3, -1/3, alpha(m_x) formula, T(k)=[1+(alpha k)^2nu]^-5/nu with nu=1.12, k<5 h/Mpc range, k_hm=0.325/alpha for 3.1/3.3/4.1/5.7 keV, alternative DW mappings (half-mode, Bozek/Murgia, Abazajian) table and spread in keV and percent, and <p/T> (mean momentum over temperature) check vs analytic lambda_FS. Blocked by tool budget, not physics.
