**Blocked — Quantify BBN/CMB Delta N_eff and Yp/D/H shifts for DW grid and test eV-scale SBL anomaly thermalization control.** Tool budget (10 calls) exhausted before read_arxiv_chunk/cite for X-ray diffuse background limit; web_search identified Dessert+2020 and Roach+2020 but no verbatim quote retrieved. Direction d-09 quantified BBN/CMB Delta N_eff and Yp/D/H shifts for DW sterile neutrinos and tested the eV-scale SBL anomaly as a thermalization control. The sterile-nu server was confirmed to return Delta N_eff, Omega_s h^2, Yp, D/H, Li7, lifetime and free-streaming (describe_sterile_nu_tools). A 35-point DW grid (masses 7.1, 20, 22, 29, 45 keV x mixings 1e-12 to 1e-8) gave Delta N_eff 6e-06 to 0.27 and Omega_s h^2 0.00047 to 130.9; none were BBN-excluded at 95% (Delta chi^2 vs SM -0.002 to -1.15, limit Delta N_eff <0.55), 28/35 overclose (Omega_s h^2 >0.12). The 7.1 keV sin^2 2theta=7e-11 point gave Delta N_eff=0.00043, Omega_s h^2=0.033 (27.5% of DM), Yp=0.24682, D/H=2.44e-5, allowed. A 5-point f_s~1 zip grid (sin^2 2.5e-10 to 6.4e-12) gave Delta N_eff 0.00017 to 0.00155 and Omega_s h^2 0.083 to 0.118 (f_s 0.69-0.98), all BBN-allowed, confirming keV DW DM contributes negligible extra radiation. Files: sterile_nu_grid_DW_230529.csv and sterile_nu_grid_DW_c49937.csv in runs/261107_183057. BBN impact plot (Figure 27, bbn_vs_neff.png/pdf) shows Yp and D/H vs N_eff: SM at N_eff=3.044 Yp=0.24682 D/H=2.4433e-5, fully thermalized sterile at N_eff=4.044 Yp=0.25956 D/H=2.7769e-5 (3.7 sigma above observed Yp=0.2449+/-0.004), slopes dYp/dN_eff=0.0135 d(D/H)/dN_eff=0.33e-5, BBN 95% limit Delta N_eff <0.548. SBL anomaly benchmark (Delta m^2=1.3 eV^2, sin^2 2theta=0.42, m_s~1.14 eV) predicts Delta N_eff=1.0 (N_eff=4.044), Omega_s h^2=29.3 (overcloses), BBN Delta chi^2=23.1 vs SM (excluded at 95%), 6.2 sigma tension with Planck N_eff=2.99+/-0.17 (CMB-S4 33 sigma). X-ray lines: 7.1 keV (E=3.55 keV, sin^2=7e-11) decay rate 1.72e-28 s^-1 lifetime 5.8e27 s fluxes 3.28 (MW center), 4.8e-04 (M31), 2.5e-05 (Perseus) ph/s/cm2 whole-halo f_DM=1; 20 keV f_s~1 (E=10 keV, sin^2=2.8e-11) rate 1.22e-26 s^-1 lifetime 8.2e25 s fluxes 82.6, 0.012, 6.3e-04; both flagged excluded by NuSTAR M31 (Roach+2020) and XMM blank sky (Dessert+2020). What was not done: verbatim citable quote and .bib entry for X-ray background limits (read_arxiv_chunk/cite) - tool budget exhausted after web_search identified arXiv:2003.03368.
