**Blocked — Build the final quantitative DW exclusion: f_s=1 line from sterile-nu tools vs Lyman-alpha mapped floors and digitized X-ray sin^2(2theta) limits, with binding constraint per mass.** X-ray limit curves are PDF-only tikz/pgfplots with no arXiv HTML rendering (2207.04572 returned no figures; 1908.09037 and 1609.00667 returned only sky-map/aperture figures), requiring manual PDF digitization, and tool budget (10 calls) was exhausted before table/plot/citation steps could run. Direction d-06 asked for a quantitative Dodelson-Widrow (non-resonant oscillation production) exclusion with f_s=1 line versus Lyman-alpha and X-ray limits. What was established: the sterile-nu tool assumes pure DW production, relativistic at Big Bang Nucleosynthesis, with Delta N_eff (extra radiation) from relic density and BBN fit valid for N_eff 2.044-6.044 and m_s below ~100 keV. A 5-point grid at sin^2(2theta)=1e-12 gave Omega_s h^2 (relic density) 0.0004715 at 7.1 keV, 0.003041 at 20 keV, 0.00361 at 22 keV, 0.005936 at 29 keV, 0.01309 at 45 keV, implying f_s=1 (100% of dark matter, Omega_s h^2=0.12) mixings 2.55e-10, 3.95e-11, 3.32e-11, 2.02e-11, 9.17e-12 respectively, saved to /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-lyman-wdm/runs/261107_183057/sterile_nu_grid_DW_bc0526.csv. The 3.5 keV line benchmark (7.1 keV, 7e-11) gives Omega_s h^2=0.033 (27.5% of dark matter), Delta N_eff=0.00043, Yp=0.24682, D/H=2.44e-5, lifetime 5.8e27 s, free-streaming 151 kpc, BBN allowed. The tool flags the 20 keV f_s=1 point (3.95e-11, E_gamma=10 keV, lifetime 5.8e25 s) as excluded by NuSTAR M31 (Roach+2020). What ran: describe_sterile_nu_tools, predict_sterile_nu_grid, predict_sterile_nu, predict_sterile_nu_xray_line locally; get_paper_figures on 2207.04572, 1908.09037, 1609.00667. What was not done: digitized X-ray sin^2(2theta) limits at 7.1, 20, 22, 29, 45 keV, f_s,max_Xray for tool vs Abazajian/ALS normalisations, Lyman-alpha mixed-DM overlay (0812.0010, 2504.06367), binding-constraint table, references.bib entry for 2207.04572, and exclusion plot. Figures retrieved were only sky-map/aperture plots (1908.09037 Fig.2, 1609.00667 Figs.3-4), not limit curves.
