**Blocked — Cross-check thermal-relic to DW sterile mass mapping and quantify floor spread from alternative prescriptions.** Tool budget (10 calls) exhausted before read_text_file/read_arxiv_chunk could fetch full text of astro-ph/0501562 for quote-verified Eq.5 and alpha formula, and before Abazajian papers could be retrieved for alternative mapping coefficients; only figure captions extracted. Direction d-07 asked to cross-check thermal-relic WDM (warm dark matter, a light thermal particle that erases small-scale structure) to DW sterile neutrino (Dodelson-Widrow, non-resonant oscillation production) mass mapping and quantify spread. What was established: Viel 2005 Eq.5 m_s = 4.43 keV * (m_WDM/1 keV)^{4/3} gives DW floors 20.0 keV for 3.1 keV, 21.8 keV for 3.3 keV, 29.1 keV for 4.1 keV, and 45.0 keV for 5.7 keV, matching board floors 20.2/21.9/29.3/45.4 keV within 1-2%. Sterile-nu tool free-streaming lengths (distance particles stream and erase structure) at sin^2 2theta=1e-10 are 53.2 kpc at 20.2 keV, 36.7 kpc at 29.3 keV, and 23.7 kpc at 45.4 keV, scaling as 1/m_s, all warm DM with BBN (Big Bang Nucleosynthesis, light-element formation) treatment valid. BBN impact at these masses is negligible: Delta N_eff (extra radiation) 0.0014 to 0.0027 (N_eff 3.045 to 3.047 vs SM 3.044), Yp (helium mass fraction) 0.24683-0.24685 (observed 0.2449 +-0.004) and D/H x1e5 2.4438-2.4442 (observed 2.547 +-0.025), Delta chi2 vs SM -0.02 to -0.04, allowed at 95%. Analytic half-mode scale from Viel T(k)=[1+(alpha k)^{2nu}]^{-5/nu} with nu=1.12 gives k_1/2=0.325/alpha = 23.4 h/Mpc for 3.1 keV and 46.0 h/Mpc for 5.7 keV (lambda ~0.27 and 0.14 h^-1 Mpc), consistent in trend with tool lambda_fs but factor 2-3 offset due to definition difference. Figures 28-31 from astro-ph/0501562 show T(k) calibration and flux power suppression at /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-lyman-wdm/runs/261107_183057/figures_astro-ph_0501562/fig01_1.png etc. What ran: describe_sterile_nu_tools, predict_sterile_nu x3 locally, get_paper_figures on astro-ph/0501562, web_search. What was not done: quote-verified Viel Eq.5 coefficient and alpha(m_x) from full text, alternative DW mappings (half-mode, Bozek/Murgia, Abazajian) table and spread in keV/%, direct <p/T> (mean momentum over temperature) check, and references.bib entries; blocked by tool budget, not physics.
